{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476197-making-a-pilotable-body-to-remote-control-how-do","id":1476197,"title":"Making a pilotable body to remote control- How do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-11T01:33:49-08:00","id":1476197,"title":"Making a pilotable body to remote control- How do?","content":"I've been working on an Aberrant concept and am struggling on how to make it work in a way that will both match the idea and also not entirely suck. <br /> <br /> The core concept is a Nova reduced down to a immobile, small object due to Transformation reshaping their body. I thought it'd be an interesting concept that much of their power set was based on recreating a body for them to control and perceive through, since they can no longer do so with their own body. Potentially utilizing Bestow effects to grant the illusion that the artificial body was the actual Nova while they did their best to conceal their true nature. <br /> <br /> Problem is, the best power that seems to match that concept is Quantum Agent, but from everything I can tell, the Agent created is pretty weak. I thought maybe Quantum Construct could do it, but I'm not entirely sure that is how that power can work. <br /> <br /> Or maybe it'd best be done by a high level Q-tech item, to help get around the powers being less effective at low levels?<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure, but I'd appreciate any advice or ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T01:47:17-08:00","id":1476198,"title":"","content":"You can do reverse, you create an Agent to be your body, the one you left behind, and you become the newly created agent during the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T05:12:08-08:00","id":1476202,"title":"","content":"Well, you're basically creating a Nova who is incredibly hard to kill, because your actual body is hard to find. It should be really expensive. You could probably build a Q-Tech device which looks like an iron lung and have that generate the Agent instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T12:14:17-08:00","id":1476221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476197-making-a-pilotable-body-to-remote-control-how-do?p=1476198#post1476198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do reverse, you create an Agent to be your body, the one you left behind, and you become the newly created agent during the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite sure what you mean by this. As far as I am aware, you can't swap bodies with an Agent?<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Well, you're basically creating a Nova who is incredibly hard to kill, because your actual body is hard to find. It should be really expensive. You could probably build a Q-Tech device which looks like an iron lung and have that generate the Agent instead.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This is fair, I'm less worried about expense and more concerned about getting a result that doesn't require Quantum rating to be absurdly high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T14:14:39-08:00","id":1476225,"title":"","content":"The Adventure! era villain known as the Ubiquitous Dragon could apparently make permanent Quantum Agents, and swap his mind between those bodies to run his global crime empire. He obviously had some unique Tags applied to the Power.<br /> <br /> You could also go the route of Bloat from the Wild Cards novels, and limit your constructs so they can't travel too far from your real body. This keeps you from becoming effectively unkillable because there is no reasonable way for enemies to find your true body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 03-11-2022, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T03:26:09-08:00","id":1476267,"title":"","content":"So, exploring multiple avenues for this concept, and was wondering if anyone could explain how large VARGs work? Reading through the Aeon Expansion book, I can't quite understand them. They are large enough that they are more vehicles than armor, so how do you determine the Might/Dexterity/Stamina of it? If it punches something, I assume you aren't using the Might of the pilot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T11:19:19-08:00","id":1476278,"title":"","content":"If you're looking at \u00c6on material, you might want to look at the Qin (detailed in Distant Worlds). They're a small, vaguely octopus-like alien race that rides around in biosuits: humanoid (and in the case of Infiltration biosuits, often human-looking) biotech vehicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T13:33:05-08:00","id":1476281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476197-making-a-pilotable-body-to-remote-control-how-do?p=1476278#post1476278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking at \u00c6on material, you might want to look at the Qin (detailed in Distant Worlds). They're a small, vaguely octopus-like alien race that rides around in biosuits: humanoid (and in the case of Infiltration biosuits, often human-looking) biotech vehicles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for pointing those out, though it seems like it just has the Qin use its own physical attributes for the biosuit despite it being an external organism? Which mechanically I can understand, but it just seems kind of weird. <br /> <br /> I'm still trying to figure out VARGs too. VARGs have melee weapons, but I can't find anything on how to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T15:28:20-08:00","id":1476290,"title":"","content":"For your original concept, I'd write up the character as if he <i>was</i> the \u201cpiloted body\u201d, then define a unique Transformation a la Puella Magi Madoka Magica: a High-Level variation of Power Loss, where the character is rendered immobile and effectively unconscious if separated from his \u201ctalisman\u201d \u2014 with the dirty secret being that he <i>is</i> the \u201ctalisman\u201d. <br /> <br /> Another possibility would be a creative use of Transformation (the Quantum Power) by inventing a pair of Negative Power Tag for it: an \u201cinflexible\u201d tag that only allows you to switch between two configurations, one representing your actual form, and the other representing your robot body; and another that specifies that both forms technically exist at all times, but you can only control the piloted body when you're \u201cwearing\u201d it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T17:39:37-08:00","id":1476298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476197-making-a-pilotable-body-to-remote-control-how-do?p=1476290#post1476290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your original concept, I'd write up the character as if he <i>was</i> the \u201cpiloted body\u201d, then define a unique Transformation a la Puella Magi Madoka Magica: a High-Level variation of Power Loss, where the character is rendered immobile and effectively unconscious if separated from his \u201ctalisman\u201d \u2014 with the dirty secret being that he <i>is</i> the \u201ctalisman\u201d.<br /> <br /> Another possibility would be a creative use of Transformation (the Quantum Power) by inventing a pair of Negative Power Tag for it: an \u201cinflexible\u201d tag that only allows you to switch between two configurations, one representing your actual form, and the other representing your robot body; and another that specifies that both forms technically exist at all times, but you can only control the piloted body when you're \u201cwearing\u201d it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll keep this ideas in my backpocket, but is there any chance you know how the physical attributes of VARGs work? That information is currently in my head for a current idea I have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T19:48:16-08:00","id":1476305,"title":"","content":"A Varg would use it's size scale as might scale in any instance where lifting, punching, etc would be involved. I think where you may run into trouble with your concept is that the Nova would probably loose access to their other powers while their conciousness was transmitted into another body. Most of the ways I can think of would end up that way. The Q Agent power would give the external body some powers (but probably less than a full character), but would require a high Quantum rating. I suspect the reason this build is difficult to do is because allowing a PC full access to all of their power while in the field with no actual personal danger is a little OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T20:01:04-08:00","id":1476308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476197-making-a-pilotable-body-to-remote-control-how-do?p=1476305#post1476305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Varg would use it's size scale as might scale in any instance where lifting, punching, etc would be involved. I think where you may run into trouble with your concept is that the Nova would probably loose access to their other powers while their conciousness was transmitted into another body. Most of the ways I can think of would end up that way. The Q Agent power would give the external body some powers (but probably less than a full character), but would require a high Quantum rating. I suspect the reason this build is difficult to do is because allowing a PC full access to all of their power while in the field with no actual personal danger is a little OP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That figures out the Scale, but if you are rolling to hit something, how do you determine your dice pool? I'm not terribly worried about the rest, I can think of plenty of ideas to make it work in the manner I want and works with my GM. My primary hurdle is just figuring out how to generate bodies and figure out their dice pools before any other quantum powers or things are involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3052-blackshade10","name":"blackshade10","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T21:55:01-08:00","id":1476315,"title":"","content":"The roll would be a piloting roll. So you could either use pilot (your ability to use the controls to make the bot do what you want), or if it is a more direct mental connection you might use close combat or athletics depending on what you are doing. In the latter case I'd probably use the Mental Attribute (so Intellect when might would be involved and Cunning for Dex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}